// Plan 221.1 (D186-амендмент) [M-interp-numeric-fallback-silent-garbage] NEG —
// bare `"${p}"` (Display: no spec, or a rich `Spec` whose kind != Debug)
// interpolation of a user record type WITHOUT `#impl(Display)` must be a
// COMPILE ERROR, not silent numeric-cast garbage.
//
// Root cause fixed here: emit_c.rs's interpolation lowering has a
// LAST-RESORT fallback (~42903, `nova_int_to_str((nova_int)(v))`) for any
// non-primitive expr that reaches bare Display with no `str.from`/`to_str`/
// `@display` route — it silently printed the record's heap address as a
// decimal integer. D186 gate_on_impl=true already means "no `#impl(Display)`
// ⇒ no display method" for the auto-derive synthesis path; this test pins
// that already-established absence surfacing as an HONEST compile error
// (`E_INTERP_NO_DISPLAY`) instead of degrading to garbage output at runtime.
// rustc precedent: `Display` is never auto-derived — a missing impl is a
// compile error, not a best-effort fallback.
//
// See spec/decisions/02-types.md#d186 (amendment) for the rule.
// Siblings: d186_interp_no_display_pos.nv (has `#impl(Display)` — works),
// d186_interp_debug_always_works_pos.nv (`${p:?}` — Debug auto-derive,
// gate_on_impl=false, always available regardless of `#impl`).
//
// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E_INTERP_NO_DISPLAY

module neg.d186_interp_no_display_neg

type NoDisplayPoint { x int, y int }

fn bad() -> str {
    ro p = NoDisplayPoint { x: 1, y: 2 }
    "${p}"
}
